1
00:00:00,475 --> 00:00:01,150
Make a column

2
00:00:01,150 --> 00:00:02,500
twice as tall,

3
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:03,113
and it carries

4
00:00:03,113 --> 00:00:04,012
only a quarter

5
00:00:04,012 --> 00:00:04,975
of the load.

6
00:00:06,050 --> 00:00:07,200
Two columns.

7
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:08,000
Same section,

8
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,000
same material.

9
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:09,800
One is twice

10
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:10,725
as long.

11
00:00:11,850 --> 00:00:12,750
Load them up.

12
00:00:12,750 --> 00:00:13,425
The long one

13
00:00:13,425 --> 00:00:14,587
bows out sideways

14
00:00:14,587 --> 00:00:15,262
first.

15
00:00:15,262 --> 00:00:16,450
That's buckling.

16
00:00:17,545 --> 00:00:18,870
Euler's formula.

17
00:00:18,870 --> 00:00:19,658
The buckling load

18
00:00:19,658 --> 00:00:20,508
is pi squared

19
00:00:20,508 --> 00:00:21,170
E I,

20
00:00:21,170 --> 00:00:22,033
over K L,

21
00:00:22,033 --> 00:00:22,920
squared.

22
00:00:24,065 --> 00:00:25,440
Length is squared.

23
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:25,990
Double it,

24
00:00:25,990 --> 00:00:26,440
and you get

25
00:00:26,440 --> 00:00:27,678
one over four.

26
00:00:27,678 --> 00:00:28,328
A quarter of

27
00:00:28,328 --> 00:00:29,440
the capacity.

28
00:00:30,510 --> 00:00:31,822
Tall and slender?

29
00:00:31,822 --> 00:00:32,373
Brace it,

30
00:00:32,373 --> 00:00:33,460
or go bigger.

31
00:00:33,460 --> 00:00:34,135
Save this for

32
00:00:34,135 --> 00:00:34,972
your next column

33
00:00:34,972 --> 00:00:35,610
check.
